From 3d5a1483fb8583e24ea264eb9f1b8a0eef236eb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:21:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Outputs of failing points, conversions, copies and mass
 density

- point by point, with values gathered in the workspace, the tangent
  operator blocks and the outputs of a post-processing of a point where
  the computations failed are no longer written (they received the values
  of the previous point), as by the computations on batches. The tangent
  operator blocks of a failing point are documented as unspecified.
- conversions of the finite strain stresses and tangent operators on
  views: the output is checked (number of points, number of components,
  distinct values) and the material data view is checked; FieldView
  overloads on the material data managers.
- FieldOperations::copy: two empty views are accepted whatever their
  extents, and two views describing the same values are recognized from
  the strides of the dimensions whose extent is greater than one.
- the mass density is required to compute the speed of sound with a
  behaviour generated by the generic-parallel interface, and is reported
  as missing by MGIS. A mass density held by a material data manager on
  the host and not accessible by the behaviour is reported as such.
